Journey: Rejecting a claim asks for confirmation, notifies the customer and publishes the decision
Id: reject-with-confirmation
Tags: @backoffice @claims @regression @kafka @email
Role: adjuster
Risk: 4
Requirements: ADJ-5, NOTIF-3, EVT-3

Run code "steps/claims.steps.ts#seedClaim" with policyId="POL-M-200455", type="THEFT", amount="640" as seeded
Set variable claimId to seeded.claimId
Start listening on Kafka topic "larkspur.claims.events" on events as decisions

Log in
Open ${BACKOFFICE_URL}/claims/${claimId}
  Expect the page contains "Review claim ${claimId}"
Select "Policy exclusion" from @ClaimDesk.reason

# Dismissing the confirmation keeps the claim open
Dismiss the next confirm dialog
Click @ClaimDesk.reject
Expect a confirm dialog saying "Reject claim ${claimId}? The customer will be notified." appeared
Expect @ClaimDesk.status has text "In review"

# Accepting it rejects the claim
Accept the next dialog and store it as confirmation
Click @ClaimDesk.reject
  Expect the page contains "Claim ${claimId} rejected"
Expect ${confirmation} contains "Reject claim ${claimId}?"

Wait for a message in decisions where "$.claimId" = "${claimId}" and header "event-type" = "claim.rejected" within 20 s as rejected
Expect response rejected "$.reason" equals "POLICY_EXCLUSION"
Expect no message in decisions where "$.claimId" = "${claimId}" and "$.type" = "claim.approved" within 3 s
Wait for an email to "amelia.hart@mail.larkspur.test" with subject "Claim ${claimId} decision" within 20 seconds as decision
Expect ${decision.text} contains "policy exclusion"
Get the value of query "SELECT status FROM claims WHERE id = '${claimId}'" on claims as status
Expect ${status} equals "REJECTED"
Run code "steps/claims.steps.ts#removeClaim" with claimId="${claimId}" as cleanup
